In article <1994Feb15.162543.29268@midway.uchicago.edu>,
brooks theodore giles <btgiles@midway.uchicago.edu> wrote:
>How fast should I attempt to descend?
>I usually end up dead at Exp level 5, dung. level 5.
>Am I going too fast, or am I incredibly unlucky?

Matter of playing style.  Usually, I try to keep moving down until I get a
safe supply of food (say, 2 food rations).  But I think it helps to completely
deal with all the shops you encounter (as far as pets/gold allow) before going
down deep.  Identifying potions is extremely dangerous to do by quaffing (
hallucination kills me every time) before you have a means of counteracting
the effect (u.horn/PoEH), but scrolls are safe to identify (dump all potions/
scrolls/spellbooks first, and take off your armor, until you have identified
fire/destroy armor, resp.; amnesia and punishment arent so bad).  Remain
unburdened if at all possible, and learn the ways of NetHack (including running
away from bad things in time ;-)
